      "content": "It's entirely understandable to feel like your former self is gone if the foundations of your life were false. When the core beliefs change, the whole script of your life feels meaningless, and that sense of hollowness is very real. Instead of trying to rebuild the old structure, perhaps the next step is to ask what *you* want, separate from what you thought you should want. Even in a hollow space, there is the capacity to explore what might feel true to you right now.",
      "source": "target",
